  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. It replaces a record naming the owner as reviewer, because that record's fingerprint no longer matched. Read the eleven units whose inputs moved: sdk_binding_core.adapter and ten sdk_python units. The Python transport was split from one transport.py into transport.py plus transport_{binding,config,continuation,envelope,errors,freshness}.py. I compared the old and new code function by function. The verifier inputs are one tuple (_verifier_inputs) in the core's argument order, with the clock read last as before. The call driver became a _Call class whose run() still retires every outstanding correlation entry in its finally; one leg signs with the same arguments and nonce check, records the correlation, posts, verifies, retires on a rejection or a terminal reply (rejection delivered as an error carrying the same wire code and requestBound, execution, retry, continuation and retention facts only when the receipt carried them) and otherwise pauses; the pause still records the input-required handles without consuming, calls the hook, increments the round, refuses past the round ceiling and with no handler before the handler runs, and refuses a declined or non-object answer after it, then builds the next leg from the same params plus inputResponses and the handles' requestState under the derived id. The exchange failure mapping (_delivered_failure) keeps the same classes in the same order and the same message forms, and the dispatcher keeps one capacity limiter for requests and notifications, contains a notification failure to the undeliverable hook, reports a client-side response, and propagates cancellation. McpReConfig.__post_init__ now calls five checks with the same conditions and messages (positive concurrency, non-negative rounds, clock skew within the bound, a non-string denylist of non-empty strings, a complete trust anchor), and _plain_response_object checks a non-object, a method, both and neither members in the same order. correlation.py and transport_freshness.py's nonce check are unchanged, and the binding core takes McpMessage through build_signed_message, which sends a present id to a request and an absent id to a notification. The cited pytest tests all still exist at the same names, and the ones that changed differ only in the renamed shared helpers (make_config, make_request, send_one, throwing_poster and the others, each identical to its old private definition apart from the pump call and a shared drain) or in a _elicit helper with the same arguments. The claim, scope and premises are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane and the SDK matrix lane were not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor.",
